    54	## Addendum B (pre-registered 2026-11-06T01:03Z, BEFORE arm-B results exist; dec 056 item 6 = dec 055 item 6 original scope)
    55	Goal: a timeout never yields an empty source diff. Arm B's prompt asks for an early edit (system.md l.14) but a prompt can't enforce it.
    56	Addendum B looks for a structural mechanism inside what the bundle can express (agent.yaml tools, agent_tool sub-agents, skills,
    57	eval_config caps).
    58	Facts: the harness collects the workspace diff on cap/overflow/exception only if submit_patch was NOT called; a submit_patch with an empty
    59	snapshot freezes the empty patch (plan 005 header). So "empty on timeout" = no edit landed, and "empty on submit" = premature submit.
    60	Candidate mechanisms (choose ONE by a dated line here BEFORE any run, after a CPU feasibility check of the ADK schema, codex-ask):
    61	 M1 localize-then-edit: the code_analyzer agent_tool (same model, read-only) returns file + symbol + a concrete replacement under its own
    62	    call/turn cap if ADK supports one; the root prompt makes applying it the next action, refinement after.
    63	 M2 provisional-edit checkpoint: a skill/tool-script step that the prompt schedules at a fixed call index and that lands the current best
    64	    edit (no-op if a source diff already exists); refinement after.
    65	 M3 submit guard: a submit_patch precondition (via get_status / git diff --stat in the prompt flow) so an empty or test-only diff is never
    66	    frozen; combinable with M1 or M2.
    67	Honest limit: a non-empty wrong diff scores the same as an empty one (0). The benefit is only the pass probability of a landed best-guess
    68	edit. This addendum measures landing, not correctness.
    69	Design: same 8 ids (eval/plans/004-gpu-retime-ids.txt), same plan-006 kernel/flags, cap 4.0, 40 calls/50 turns, conc 1, k=1. Baseline =
    70	whichever of arm A / arm B has fewer empties (ties -> arm B). Only the chosen mechanism differs from that baseline. Needs a Kaggle quota or
    71	GPU approval (separate request).
    72	Primary: # timeouts with an empty source diff (agent.patch 0 bytes or test/config-only). Secondary: empty count, paired discordants vs
    73	baseline + exact sign test, first-ok-edit call index, gates a/b/d/e.
    74	Decision rule: PASS = gates a,b,d,e pass AND empty-on-timeout = 0 AND empty total <= baseline empty total AND C-empty-only = 0.
    75	 -> fold into the next candidate (31b, then the e4b port), codex-review. FAIL on any part -> one revision, then stop (two-strike).
